Template: debian-installer/next-partitioner/title
Type: text
Description: Partition disks

Template: next-partitioner/root
Type: string
Description: for internal use only
 The root partition, as the installed system will name it.

Template: next-partitioner/boot
Type: string
Description: for internal use only
 The boot partition, as the installer names it.

Template: next-partitioner/disk
Type: select
Choices-C: ${CHOICES_C}
Choices: ${CHOICES}
Description: Disk to install Debian on:
 The disk is given a NeXT disk label with three partitions: the root file
 system, swap, and a small boot partition for the kernel.  Everything on it
 is erased.
 .
 Disks are named as the kernel will name them once the installer is gone,
 if it was started from a disk of its own.

Template: next-partitioner/swap
Type: string
Default: 256
Description: Swap space (MB):
 A NeXT has little memory, and Debian needs swap on it: 256 MB is enough
 for a 64 MB machine.  0 leaves swap out.

Template: next-partitioner/bad-swap
Type: error
Description: Not a size
 The swap size must be a whole number of megabytes, from 0 to 4096.

Template: next-partitioner/confirm
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Erase ${DISK} and install Debian on it?
 ${DISK} (${INFO}) will get a new NeXT disk label:
 .
 ${LAYOUT}
 .
 Everything now on the disk will be lost.

Template: next-partitioner/no-disks
Type: error
Description: No disk found
 There is no SCSI disk to install on, other than the installer's own.

Template: next-partitioner/failed
Type: error
Description: Partitioning failed
 ${ERROR}
 .
 Check /var/log/syslog, or the fourth virtual console, for details.

Template: next-partitioner/progress/title
Type: text
Description: Partitioning ${DISK}

Template: next-partitioner/progress/label
Type: text
Description: Writing the NeXT disk label...

Template: next-partitioner/progress/mkfs
Type: text
Description: Making the ext4 file system...

Template: next-partitioner/progress/swap
Type: text
Description: Making the swap space...

Template: next-partitioner/progress/mount
Type: text
Description: Mounting the file system...
